    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11935" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cunnus</span></b> , i, m.
		cf. Sanscr. çushi, ditch; Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυσός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the female pudenda</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i><span class="en">Mart. 1,
				90, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 72,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 81, 4</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Auct. Priap. 28,
			5</span></i>.—Also of animals: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					96, 6</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of the person, <i>an
				unchaste</i>
			
			<i>female</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				2, 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 3, 107</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Auct.
				Priap. 69, 1 al.</span></i>—As an obscene word,
			avoided acc. to <i><span class="en">Cic. Or. 45, 154</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 9,
				22, 3</span></i>.</div>
